  "maintenance": [
    {
      "date": "2026-10-19",
      "change": "Built: 135 variants; the Target layer was re-centered after creation (it sat 28 px up-left) and checked centered in the three densities; a hidden Loading indicator was added to the 108 non-loading variants so that an instance can show loading + disabled."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-10-20",
      "change": "Specification 219:1828: the gaps of the example rows (Compact toolbar, Editor toolbar, table rows, Card header, Dark toolbar, Player, Pair sm/md/lg) are bound to space/control/gap/{size}, and the sizing text states the compact sm exception (4 px apart, targets reaching 4 px into the neighbor's square). The master is unchanged."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-10-26",
      "change": "Icon slot (authoring/adapters/figma/icon-slot-migrate.plugin.js): the nested, exposed Icon (sm/md/lg) is replaced in the 135 variants by the Phosphor glyph itself, width and height bound to size/icon/{size}, fill button/foreground, hidden in the loading variants, behind the new instance-swap property Icon#254:0. User decision at the wave 1 Figma parity review (2026-10-26): a component imposes the size of its icon, so the designer chooses the glyph only; an exposed nested Icon showed its Size property. 168 specification instances re-given their glyph; 18 loading instances had their glyph shown again by the swap (Figma shows a hidden glyph when it is swapped) and were hidden again. Description and texts updated; parity re-measured: the 18 hashes are those of computed.json (specification pixel-identical before the text change)."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-10-29",
      "change": "Library pages (user decision): the master moved to the section IconButton of the Actions library page (IDs kept, instances linked; library-pages.plugin.js); the component page keeps the specification, which now links to the section (spec-master-links.plugin.js)."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-10-30",
      "change": "Library page layout (user request): the Actions page opens with the overview frame (379:982: description, isometric masonry cover of live instances, a card per component); the section IconButton starts with a Section header (379:2891: summary, specification link, properties) and the master sits under it (family-pages.plugin.js; IDs of the masters unchanged). The specification's link to the master moved to the top right of the title row (367:8; spec-header-links.plugin.js, replacing spec-master-links.plugin.js); Documentation and Contract links follow at the first publication."
